### D. Surprise Memory (Aktív Learning)

**core_relational/surprise_memory.zig**:
```zig
pub const SurpriseMemory = struct {
    episodic_buffer: []EpisodicTrace,
    surprise_threshold: f32,

    pub fn recordInference(self: *SurpriseMemory, 
                          input: *Tensor, 
                          output: *Tensor,
                          confidence: f32) !void {
        const expected_output = try self.predictFromMemory(input);
        defer expected_output.deinit();

        const surprise = try self.computeSurprise(&expected_output, output);

        if (surprise > self.surprise_threshold) {
            // Váratlan eredmény → MEGJEGYEZZÜK
            const trace = EpisodicTrace{
                .input_hash = try self.hashInput(input),
                .output = try output.clone(),
                .surprise_score = surprise,
                .timestamp = std.time.timestamp(),
            };

            try self.episodic_buffer.append(trace);

            // Prioritizált replay (high-surprise episódok)
            if (self.episodic_buffer.len > 1000) {
                try self.consolidate();  // Régi + unalmas → feledés
            }
        }
    }

    fn computeSurprise(self: *SurpriseMemory, 
                      expected: *Tensor, 
                      actual: *Tensor) !f32 {
        // KL divergencia (információelméleti meglepetés)
        var kl: f32 = 0.0;
        for (expected.data, actual.data) |e, a| {
            kl += a * std.math.log(a / (e + 1e-8));
        }
        return kl;
    }
};
```

**AGI jellemző**: Az emberi memória nem minden részletet tárol – csak a **meglepő** eseményeket. Ez az "encoding specificity principle" (Tulving, 1974)[github:kollarsandor/dontyoujuststop].

